   "grammarNote": {
    "en": "Wedding speeches in Japan: strictly avoid taboo words suggesting separation such as kireru (to break), wakareru (to part), owaru (to end); aim for about 3 minutes — open with congratulations, share one memory of the couple, close with blessings. Writing it out and rehearsing many times is the standard.",
